# minigame-select -- the port's own walk into Mini-Game mode.
#
# The mode-select ring (src/REL/modeseldll/modesel.c:113) opens on an A whose
# frame depends on how long the new-file card scene ran, and a stick push that
# lands before it opens is simply lost -- ten pushes spread over 600 frames all
# were.  So the walk stops trying to find that frame and makes every A press a
# candidate: A, then two pushes right 20 and 50 frames later, then the next A
# 90 frames on.  Whichever A opens the ring, the two pushes that follow it are
# inside, and the A after that accepts Mini-Game.  A push that lands on the
# file select or the card scene moves a cursor whose choice does not matter.

at 700 6 START
at 750 6 START
at 800 6 START
at 850 6 START
at 900 6 START
at 950 6 START
at 1000 6 START
at 1050 6 START
at 1100 6 START

at 1160 6 A
at 1180 6 dstk:RIGHT
